---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import family from '../assets/family.jpg';
import Heading from '../components/Heading.astro';
import Link from '../components/Link.astro';
import Paragraph from '../components/Paragraph.astro';
import { intercalate, shuffleArray, yearsSince } from '../utils';
import Tooltip from './Tooltip.astro';

const FEATURES = [
  { text: 'software engineer', href: '#software-engineer' },
  {
    text: 'aspiring functional programming guru',
    href: '#aspiring-functional-programming-guru',
  },
  { text: 'software educator', href: '#software-educator' },
  { text: 'dad of three', href: '#dad-of-three' },
  { text: 'occasional cinephile' },
  { text: 'reader of books' },
  { text: 'listener of music' },
];
const START_OF_PROFESSIONAL_CAREER = new Date('2007-08-01');

const shuffledFeatures = shuffleArray(FEATURES);
const yearsOfProfessionalCareer = yearsSince(START_OF_PROFESSIONAL_CAREER);
---

<article>
  <div class="w-full bg-linear-to-b from-blue-800 to-indigo-900 pb-24">
    <section class="mx-auto p-4 mb-48 max-w-prose text-lg md:text-2xl md:p-8">
      <h1
        class="font-serif text-7xl font-bold mt-36 mb-16 text-yellow-300 text-shadow-lg sm:mt-56 sm:text-9xl md:text-[9rem] md:mb-36 xl:max-w-fit xl:mx-auto"
      >
        Abbe Keultjes
      </h1>
      <Paragraph variant="large" class="mx-auto">
        In no particular order:
        {
          intercalate(
            shuffledFeatures.map((feature) =>
              feature.href ? <Link href={feature.href}>{feature.text}</Link> : feature.text,
            ),
            ', ',
          )
        }.
      </Paragraph>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto p-4 mb-24 max-w-prose text-lg md:text-2xl md:p-8">
      <Heading id="software-engineer">Software engineer</Heading>
      <Paragraph>
        I’ve been writing software professionally for over
        <Tooltip
          content={`Since ${START_OF_PROFESSIONAL_CAREER.toLocaleDateString('en-UK', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long' })}`}
          ><time
            datetime={START_OF_PROFESSIONAL_CAREER.toISOString()}
            class="underline underline-offset-4 decoration-dotted">{yearsOfProfessionalCareer} years</time
          ></Tooltip
        >, with more than a decade focused on frontend development as a consultant. I’m known for delivering robust,
        well-considered implementations, combining a keen eye for detail with a thorough approach to both code and
        problem-solving. My primary languages are JavaScript and TypeScript.
      </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph>
        My work combines hands-on development with careful attention to software architecture, with functional
        programming playing a central role. I also enjoy coaching fellow programmers on coding practices, communication,
        and sharing knowledge effectively.
      </Paragraph>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto p-4 mb-24 max-w-prose text-lg md:text-2xl md:p-8">
      <Heading id="aspiring-functional-programming-guru">Aspiring functional<br />programming guru</Heading>
      <Paragraph>
        Code should be simple (<Link
          href="https://youtu.be/SxdOUGdseq4?si=uUW2jW2kYT_SDuYB"
          openInNewTab
          tooltip="Rich Hickey on YouTube">not easy</Link
        >), maintainable, and communicate its intent clearly. That’s why I strongly prefer the functional programming
        paradigm: controlled side effects, immutable data, and functions as building blocks. This approach helps me
        build systems that are easier to reason about, test, and evolve over time.
      </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph>
        I’m drawn toward any language with a strong foundation in functional programming (F#, Haskell, etc.), but I have
        a soft spot for Clojure and its community.
      </Paragraph>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto p-4 mb-24 max-w-prose text-lg md:text-2xl md:p-8">
      <Heading id="software-educator">Software educator</Heading>
      <Paragraph>
        I’m a software educator with experience designing and teaching workshops and talks on modern JavaScript and
        functional programming. I enjoy breaking down complex concepts into practical, approachable lessons for
        audiences ranging from beginners to experienced developers.
      </Paragraph>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="bg-slate-900 pt-12">
    <div class="mx-auto p-4 max-w-prose text-lg md:text-2xl md:p-8">
      <Heading id="dad-of-three" variant="indigo">Dad of three</Heading>
      <Paragraph>And a husband to one ❤️.</Paragraph>
    </div>
    <Image
      src={family}
      alt="Abbe Keultjes and his family"
      title="I’m the second from the right 😉"
      layout="full-width"
      class="z-10 relative"
    />
  </section>
</article>
